1
00:00:15,180 --> 00:00:16,897
Destiny. Fate. Dreams.

2
00:00:16,980 --> 00:00:21,140
These unstoppable ideals are
held deep in the heart of man.

3
00:00:21,540 --> 00:00:24,937
As long as there are people
who seek freedom in this life,

4
00:00:25,020 --> 00:00:27,667
these things shall not
vanish from the earth.

5
00:00:34,680 --> 00:00:37,497
People tell me my head's in the clouds.

6
00:00:37,580 --> 00:00:40,877
I don't care what they say
because I'm dreaming of you!

7
00:00:40,960 --> 00:00:43,577
You are the treasure I found.

8
00:00:43,660 --> 00:00:46,657
So bright, so bold, and so elusive.

9
00:00:46,740 --> 00:00:48,697
It's hard to look away.

10
00:00:48,780 --> 00:00:51,857
Even though it's blinding me.

11
00:00:51,940 --> 00:00:55,697
There are no words to
describe how I feel inside.

12
00:00:55,780 --> 00:00:58,020
I'm really, really stuck on you.

13
00:00:59,220 --> 00:01:02,537
I have to follow my dreams,
however crazy they seem!

14
00:01:02,620 --> 00:01:05,597
And I won't stop till I
get there, you will see!

15
00:01:05,680 --> 00:01:08,877
You're all I need to have
the strength to believe.

16
00:01:08,960 --> 00:01:12,220
We live in wonderland.

17
00:01:17,880 --> 00:01:21,117
I'm gonna follow my dreams,
however crazy they seem!

18
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:24,157
I'm gonna share them
with you, a love so true.

19
00:01:24,240 --> 00:01:27,557
You're all I want,
together we can move on.

20
00:01:27,640 --> 00:01:29,917
We'll live how we want to.

21
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:32,037
There is no limit to us.

22
00:01:32,120 --> 00:01:33,537
We have the power of love.

23
00:01:33,620 --> 00:01:36,617
We don't want to live ordinary life.

24
00:01:36,700 --> 00:01:39,777
We have a chance to live in paradise.

25
00:01:39,860 --> 00:01:42,480
We'll live in one another.

26
00:01:56,080 --> 00:01:57,962
I think you've got it backwards.

27
00:01:59,200 --> 00:02:00,671
The hiding thing, I mean.

28
00:02:07,600 --> 00:02:08,880
Well, that is better.

29
00:02:09,180 --> 00:02:12,827
But it's a little late at this
point, and I can still see you.

30
00:02:13,220 --> 00:02:14,540
Shut up, lady!

31
00:02:15,460 --> 00:02:17,897
Oh, and can you tell me
how your fever's doing?

32
00:02:17,980 --> 00:02:18,810
It's choking!

33
00:02:27,520 --> 00:02:29,200
Keep it down, Chopper!

34
00:02:38,540 --> 00:02:40,897
Your fever seems to have
gone down a little bit.

35
00:02:40,980 --> 00:02:41,810
That's good.

36
00:02:43,200 --> 00:02:44,100
You happy?

37
00:02:49,380 --> 00:02:50,340
Who are you?

38
00:02:51,780 --> 00:02:53,898
Yes, it's gone down several degrees.

39
00:02:54,020 --> 00:02:55,097
Should be all right.

40
00:02:55,180 --> 00:02:58,400
I'm the only doctor
around here. Dr. Kureha.

41
00:02:58,740 --> 00:03:00,820
But you can call me Dr. Rain, okay?

42
00:03:02,160 --> 00:03:03,897
Oh, then that means we're on...

43
00:03:03,980 --> 00:03:05,862
Looking for how I stay so young?

44
00:03:06,140 --> 00:03:07,720
No, that's not it.

45
00:03:13,640 --> 00:03:16,397
Anyway, yes, you're in the
castle on the mountain.

46
00:03:16,480 --> 00:03:19,677
In that case, there were two other people
who showed up here with me, weren't there?

47
00:03:19,760 --> 00:03:22,037
Yeah, they're sleeping in the next room.

48
00:03:22,120 --> 00:03:23,000
Very deeply.

49
00:03:23,300 --> 00:03:24,640
Two real tough guys.

50
00:03:28,200 --> 00:03:30,200
This is what caused your sickness.

51
00:03:31,220 --> 00:03:32,050
Really?

52
00:03:32,600 --> 00:03:35,129
You were bitten by a
bug called the Kestia.

53
00:03:35,480 --> 00:03:39,197
It's a poisonous tick that thrives in
jungles with high heat and humidity.

54
00:03:39,280 --> 00:03:42,817
When it bites you, it introduces
a type of bacteria into your body.

55
00:03:42,900 --> 00:03:46,547
These bacteria lay dormant for
five days, causing severe pain.

56
00:03:47,380 --> 00:03:51,920
It causes a high fever, a severe
infection, myocarditis, and arteritis.

57
00:03:52,180 --> 00:03:53,010
Not pleasant.

58
00:03:53,140 --> 00:03:55,617
Given the infection's
progression in the affected area,

59
00:03:55,700 --> 00:03:58,437
I'd guess you'd been infected
for about three days now.

60
00:03:58,520 --> 00:04:00,797
The pain you'd been feeling
must have been terrible,

61
00:04:00,880 --> 00:04:04,837
but still it would have eased up in two
more days without any treatment at all.

62
00:04:04,920 --> 00:04:07,660
It would have gone away
in two days? Mm-hmm.

63
00:04:08,180 --> 00:04:12,062
You wouldn't be feeling any pain
whatsoever because you'd be dead.

64
00:04:13,200 --> 00:04:16,377
This particular infection is
known as the five-day disease.

65
00:04:16,460 --> 00:04:19,537
I had heard that Kestia had died
out over a hundred years ago,

66
00:04:19,620 --> 00:04:21,737
but I kept the antibiotic just in case.

67
00:04:21,820 --> 00:04:24,977
Where did you guys come from that
you may have been exposed to this?

68
00:04:25,060 --> 00:04:29,060
Were you walking around some ancient
jungle with your belly showing?

69
00:04:30,040 --> 00:04:30,940
No, ridiculous.

70
00:04:32,540 --> 00:04:33,370
Uh...

71
00:04:35,020 --> 00:04:37,257
Does this situation sound familiar at all?

72
00:04:37,340 --> 00:04:39,222
What a crazy girl you are, then.

73
00:04:41,040 --> 00:04:42,380
Now, stay in bed.

74
00:04:42,580 --> 00:04:45,517
The treatment for the disease
isn't completely finished yet.

75
00:04:45,600 --> 00:04:46,800
Thank you so much.

76
00:04:46,980 --> 00:04:49,037
I'll be fine as long
as my fever goes down.

77
00:04:49,120 --> 00:04:51,257
My body will take care
of itself after that.

78
00:04:51,340 --> 00:04:53,157
Well, aren't you an optimistic one?

79
00:04:53,240 --> 00:04:55,077
This disease normally takes a course of

80
00:04:55,160 --> 00:04:57,617
treatment ten days long
to successfully cure.

81
00:04:57,700 --> 00:05:00,237
Even with medicines as
advanced as mine are,

82
00:05:00,320 --> 00:05:02,917
your body will still need at least
three days to fully recuperate.

83
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:07,765
If you don't want to risk more suffering
and possibly death, get some rest, girl.

84
00:05:08,200 --> 00:05:09,640
I can't stay that long.

85
00:05:09,840 --> 00:05:12,369
We need to get Vivi
home, back to Alabasta.

86
00:05:14,700 --> 00:05:19,347
When a patient leaves this castle, it's
because she's either cured or deceased.

87
00:05:19,660 --> 00:05:21,377
You aren't going anywhere, girl.

88
00:05:21,460 --> 00:05:22,989
You better get used to it.

89
00:05:50,220 --> 00:05:52,717
He climbed this mountain
with his bare hands.

90
00:05:52,800 --> 00:05:55,740
That's almost three miles
of sheer rock to go up!

91
00:05:57,540 --> 00:06:00,077
His entire body is on
the brink of frostbite.

92
00:06:00,160 --> 00:06:02,917
What was he thinking dressing
like that for such a climb?

93
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:04,917
Draw some hot water and throw him into it.

94
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:06,857
This guy is bleeding a whole lot.

95
00:06:06,940 --> 00:06:09,700
He has six broken ribs
and a spinal fissure.

96
00:06:09,960 --> 00:06:11,257
Can I operate on him, Dr.

97
00:06:11,340 --> 00:06:12,170
E?

98
00:06:13,220 --> 00:06:16,477
Apparently the most critical of
our three patients is this girl.

99
00:06:16,560 --> 00:06:17,560
This one's dying.

100
00:06:18,180 --> 00:06:19,010
Chopper!

101
00:06:19,093 --> 00:06:22,177
Have phenocall, cardiotonic,
and thiosaline ready for me.

102
00:06:22,260 --> 00:06:23,495
She has an infection?

103
00:06:24,160 --> 00:06:27,572
Yes, and the infection isn't
from anywhere on this island.

104
00:06:33,760 --> 00:06:34,800
Don't worry, boy.

105
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:37,497
I'll make the bleeding kid
and the sick girl better.

106
00:06:37,580 --> 00:06:39,286
You can rest easy, all right?

107
00:06:40,860 --> 00:06:43,000
Those two are my friends, okay?

108
00:06:49,080 --> 00:06:50,320
I figured that kid.

109
00:06:50,520 --> 00:06:52,344
I'll save them, so don't worry.

110
00:06:52,480 --> 00:06:54,304
Chopper, let's begin treatment.

111
00:06:58,740 --> 00:07:00,920
Those two are my friends, okay?

112
00:07:03,640 --> 00:07:05,100
I'm hungry.

113
00:07:06,740 --> 00:07:08,220
So hungry.

114
00:07:13,080 --> 00:07:14,660
Need meat.

115
00:07:18,820 --> 00:07:22,237
A venison stew should be
simmered in a large pot

116
00:07:22,320 --> 00:07:25,320
for three hours until all
the meat becomes tender.

117
00:07:28,160 --> 00:07:29,000
Venison.

118
00:07:40,160 --> 00:07:41,680
Somebody help me!

119
00:07:42,200 --> 00:07:43,030
Yeah?

120
00:07:44,020 --> 00:07:45,540
Hold on, me too!

121
00:07:51,060 --> 00:07:53,766
Hold on, Luffy, let me
cook this guy up first!

122
00:08:01,600 --> 00:08:02,430
Nami!

123
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:03,830
Nami, dear!

124
00:08:03,913 --> 00:08:05,397
You look like you're all better!

125
00:08:05,480 --> 00:08:06,677
Getting there, thanks.

126
00:08:06,760 --> 00:08:07,590
Right!

127
00:08:07,673 --> 00:08:09,811
One tasty venison dish for Nami coming up!

128
00:08:13,660 --> 00:08:14,740
Come back!

129
00:08:18,260 --> 00:08:19,260
I'm impressed.

130
00:08:19,560 --> 00:08:21,557
Those guys are already up and moving.

131
00:08:21,640 --> 00:08:22,497
Yeah, they are.

132
00:08:22,580 --> 00:08:24,933
Can you tell me about this talking deer?

133
00:08:25,060 --> 00:08:26,707
Figured you'd ask about him.

134
00:08:26,920 --> 00:08:28,420
Don't run away, meat!

135
00:08:28,680 --> 00:08:29,680
Don't eat it yet!

136
00:08:35,240 --> 00:08:36,500
Leave me alone!

137
00:08:36,760 --> 00:08:37,936
His name is Chopper.

138
00:08:38,040 --> 00:08:40,981
He's just a reindeer with
a blue nose, that's all.

139
00:08:41,780 --> 00:08:44,220
But normal reindeers don't talk.

140
00:08:45,620 --> 00:08:49,377
If he's different from ordinary
reindeers in some way...

141
00:08:49,460 --> 00:08:50,940
If he's different?

142
00:08:54,300 --> 00:08:56,840
I am not food for you, okay?

143
00:08:59,100 --> 00:09:02,917
If he's different, it's just because he
ate a human, human fruit, that's all.

144
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:04,200
A human-human fruit.

145
00:09:04,460 --> 00:09:05,900
A Devil Fruit, right?

146
00:09:07,780 --> 00:09:08,610
That's right.

147
00:09:08,693 --> 00:09:09,797
He's still a reindeer,

148
00:09:09,880 --> 00:09:14,174
but now he has the abilities of a
human, like talking and walking abroad.

149
00:09:14,280 --> 00:09:16,040
No! This way!

150
00:09:16,780 --> 00:09:18,420
And also, he's a doctor.

151
00:09:18,600 --> 00:09:22,600
I taught Chopper everything that I
know about the field of medicine.

152
00:09:25,640 --> 00:09:26,700
What a shame.

153
00:09:26,920 --> 00:09:27,840
Already over?

154
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:35,353
Well, that was disappointing, wasn't it?

155
00:09:40,800 --> 00:09:41,630
Amazing.

156
00:09:42,740 --> 00:09:43,570
Right!

157
00:09:43,653 --> 00:09:44,737
Zoro, that was a good job!

158
00:09:44,820 --> 00:09:46,077
Just like I told you to do!

159
00:09:46,160 --> 00:09:46,990
Yeah!

160
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:48,830
Great!

161
00:09:48,913 --> 00:09:50,357
Now we can go over there
and look for Dalton!

162
00:09:50,440 --> 00:09:51,270
Let's go!

163
00:09:53,680 --> 00:09:54,562
Thank you, sir.

164
00:09:57,140 --> 00:09:58,600
Hurry! Dig everywhere!

165
00:10:00,440 --> 00:10:01,797
So what's going on here?

166
00:10:01,880 --> 00:10:03,137
Why are they all so worked up?

167
00:10:03,220 --> 00:10:04,657
I'll explain it all to you later.

168
00:10:04,740 --> 00:10:06,777
For now, let's just give them a hand.

169
00:10:06,860 --> 00:10:07,880
Come on, Dalton.

170
00:10:08,180 --> 00:10:09,533
Please, still be alive.

171
00:10:19,800 --> 00:10:21,477
You should be one of my crew.

172
00:10:21,560 --> 00:10:22,560
Please, old lady.

173
00:10:22,660 --> 00:10:25,072
We really need to have a doctor on board.

174
00:10:25,500 --> 00:10:28,960
Luffy, did you just call
me old lady? Yeah, right.

175
00:10:29,120 --> 00:10:30,357
That's what I said, old lady.

176
00:10:30,440 --> 00:10:33,852
If I were you, I'd be a little
more careful of what I say!

177
00:10:35,920 --> 00:10:39,420
I'm still well within my
youthful 130s, thank you.

178
00:10:40,280 --> 00:10:42,140
Jeez, you're a tough old hag.

179
00:10:44,220 --> 00:10:47,102
Are you boys really asking
me to become a pirate?

180
00:10:47,620 --> 00:10:48,796
Don't be ridiculous.

181
00:10:48,960 --> 00:10:51,617
That would be an incredible
waste of my precious time.

182
00:10:51,700 --> 00:10:54,465
Besides, I have no interest
in life on the sea.

183
00:10:54,700 --> 00:10:56,320
Those are all lame excuses.

184
00:10:56,600 --> 00:10:58,197
It's about adventure, old woman.

185
00:10:58,280 --> 00:10:59,937
Well, this one's a slow learner.

186
00:11:00,020 --> 00:11:02,667
Didn't I just tell you
to watch what you say?

187
00:11:03,040 --> 00:11:04,880
So these guys are pirates?

188
00:11:11,680 --> 00:11:12,600
Wait, food!

189
00:11:12,820 --> 00:11:14,360
Come back here! Slow down!

190
00:11:16,920 --> 00:11:17,880
Get back!

191
00:11:18,080 --> 00:11:19,477
That's enough of that, idiots!

192
00:11:19,560 --> 00:11:20,460
Whee!

193
00:11:27,080 --> 00:11:27,910
Right!

194
00:11:27,993 --> 00:11:29,057
In just a few minutes,

195
00:11:29,140 --> 00:11:32,117
I'm going to cook you a delicious
reindeer dish you'll never forget!

196
00:11:32,200 --> 00:11:33,300
I don't think so!

197
00:11:35,060 --> 00:11:38,040
I'll eat you guys first
before I let that happen!

198
00:11:38,380 --> 00:11:39,556
Let's do everything!

199
00:11:42,900 --> 00:11:46,469
She's coming!

200
00:11:47,580 --> 00:11:49,180
I don't care about food.

201
00:11:49,340 --> 00:11:51,281
I just want some peace and quiet.

202
00:11:57,660 --> 00:11:58,490
Snow?

203
00:11:58,573 --> 00:12:00,873
But that shouldn't be inside the castle.

204
00:12:01,200 --> 00:12:02,120
It's freezing.

205
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:06,176
I'll close the door.

206
00:12:06,260 --> 00:12:08,060
No, you need to stay in bed.

207
00:12:09,380 --> 00:12:11,580
After all, you still have a fever.

208
00:12:12,260 --> 00:12:13,397
I don't think so.

209
00:12:13,480 --> 00:12:15,557
It seems like it's pretty much gone now.

210
00:12:15,640 --> 00:12:16,640
I lost him.

211
00:12:17,060 --> 00:12:18,760
At least for now. Dr.

212
00:12:18,880 --> 00:12:21,297
Ene's medicine works
quickly to reduce the fever.

213
00:12:21,380 --> 00:12:23,497
But the bacteria from
the castile will still

214
00:12:23,580 --> 00:12:25,937
remain inside your body
for a little while longer.

215
00:12:26,020 --> 00:12:28,961
So just take your antibiotic
shot and stay in bed.

216
00:12:30,580 --> 00:12:32,040
Thank you. Hmm?

217
00:12:32,880 --> 00:12:36,174
You're the one who's been
taking care of me, aren't you?

218
00:12:37,960 --> 00:12:39,240
You just shut up!

219
00:12:39,560 --> 00:12:42,854
I don't eat thanks from you
or any other low-life human!

220
00:12:44,560 --> 00:12:45,580
Don't mock me!

221
00:12:45,760 --> 00:12:48,231
Oh, never mind that, I'm just being silly.

222
00:12:48,400 --> 00:12:50,780
No, seriously, I'm being such a fool.

223
00:12:52,080 --> 00:12:54,433
He's not so good at hiding his emotions.

224
00:12:59,520 --> 00:13:01,285
This castle is really strange.

225
00:13:01,540 --> 00:13:03,599
It's freezing and filled with snow.

226
00:13:07,600 --> 00:13:08,817
It's cold in here!

227
00:13:08,900 --> 00:13:12,018
Not the sharpest knife in
the drawer, are you, Luffy?

228
00:13:16,640 --> 00:13:17,820
Look at this.

229
00:13:24,580 --> 00:13:26,340
There's snow everywhere.

230
00:13:29,120 --> 00:13:33,240
And look, all the doors to the
unused rooms are frozen shut too.

231
00:13:48,160 --> 00:13:50,940
Come back here in just a moment, boys!

232
00:13:55,040 --> 00:13:56,797
I said come back here!

233
00:13:56,880 --> 00:14:00,097
You should rethink this idea about
asking the old hag to join our team.

234
00:14:00,180 --> 00:14:02,097
A real doctor doesn't
chase her patients around

235
00:14:02,180 --> 00:14:05,004
a freaky snow-filled
castle trying to kill them!

236
00:14:07,640 --> 00:14:10,300
Is it true that you guys are pirates? Yes.

237
00:14:11,480 --> 00:14:12,310
Really?

238
00:14:12,393 --> 00:14:13,223
Real pirates?

239
00:14:13,306 --> 00:14:14,136
It's real pirates.

240
00:14:14,420 --> 00:14:16,277
So you have a flag with a skull on it?

241
00:14:16,360 --> 00:14:17,737
We do, it's on our ship.

242
00:14:17,820 --> 00:14:19,997
So you're really
interested in pirates, huh?

243
00:14:20,080 --> 00:14:22,060
No, not at all! You idiot!

244
00:14:23,060 --> 00:14:23,920
Shut up!

245
00:14:25,700 --> 00:14:27,257
All right, all right, I get it.

246
00:14:27,340 --> 00:14:28,170
Now calm down.

247
00:14:30,260 --> 00:14:31,700
But one more thing.

248
00:14:32,660 --> 00:14:34,307
Do you want to come with us?

249
00:14:35,540 --> 00:14:38,246
You could come sail with
us, out on the ocean.

250
00:14:38,420 --> 00:14:39,250
Hmm?

251
00:14:39,360 --> 00:14:41,437
If you did, that would
really help me out a lot.

252
00:14:41,520 --> 00:14:42,937
If we had a doctor on this ship,

253
00:14:43,020 --> 00:14:45,057
then I wouldn't have to stay
in this place three more days,

254
00:14:45,140 --> 00:14:45,970
right?

255
00:14:46,053 --> 00:14:47,457
I think you'd have a really
good time if you came.

256
00:14:47,540 --> 00:14:48,740
No! That's crazy!

257
00:14:49,020 --> 00:14:50,608
You realize I'm a reindeer!

258
00:14:50,740 --> 00:14:53,564
I don't belong on a ship
with a bunch of humans!

259
00:14:55,440 --> 00:14:57,160
I mean, just look at me.

260
00:14:57,560 --> 00:15:01,257
I'm a reindeer, but I walk on two
legs and I talk and everything.

261
00:15:01,340 --> 00:15:03,917
Animals aren't supposed to
be able to do that stuff.

262
00:15:04,000 --> 00:15:07,941
Uh, I know, but if you're trying
to scare me off, it isn't working.

263
00:15:10,040 --> 00:15:11,400
But I have a blue nose.

264
00:15:21,560 --> 00:15:22,920
There you are, meat!

265
00:15:23,240 --> 00:15:24,420
Come here, bear!

266
00:15:26,080 --> 00:15:27,120
Come back!

267
00:15:32,480 --> 00:15:34,656
Those brats sure can run, can't they?

268
00:15:36,780 --> 00:15:39,721
I don't much like what you
were doing there, girl.

269
00:15:40,700 --> 00:15:44,197
Trying to tempt my reindeer away
from me without my permission

270
00:15:44,280 --> 00:15:45,110
What?

271
00:15:45,193 --> 00:15:48,586
I need your permission to make
a move on a man all of a sudden?

272
00:15:49,300 --> 00:15:50,697
No, I suppose you don't.

273
00:15:50,780 --> 00:15:52,957
If you want to take him
away from here, go ahead!

274
00:15:53,040 --> 00:15:56,216
But I must warn you, it won't
be as easy as you think.

275
00:15:56,300 --> 00:15:58,017
Chopper has a scar on his heart.

276
00:15:58,100 --> 00:16:00,097
A deep one my medicine can't cure.

277
00:16:00,180 --> 00:16:01,997
From the moment he was born.

278
00:16:02,080 --> 00:16:05,551
Everyone, including his parents,
turned their backs on him.

279
00:16:07,340 --> 00:16:09,337
All because he was born with a blue nose.

280
00:16:09,420 --> 00:16:12,185
He was forced to walk at
the back of the group,

281
00:16:12,280 --> 00:16:14,157
separated from the rest of the reindeer,

282
00:16:14,240 --> 00:16:16,769
even though he was just
a helpless newborn.

283
00:16:17,400 --> 00:16:19,500
Then one day he ate a Devil Fruit,

284
00:16:19,660 --> 00:16:23,307
and he became even more of an
outcast than he had been before.

285
00:16:35,520 --> 00:16:37,957
The other reindeer pressured
him to leave the herd.

286
00:16:38,040 --> 00:16:40,277
His blue nose already made him different,

287
00:16:40,360 --> 00:16:43,419
but now he wasn't like the
ordinary reindeer at all.

288
00:16:44,040 --> 00:16:46,197
Still, he was lonely and wanted friends,

289
00:16:46,280 --> 00:16:50,100
so he went down to a village
walking on two legs, as humans do.

290
00:16:51,020 --> 00:16:53,400
Hey, what is that creature over there?

291
00:16:53,660 --> 00:16:57,517
But even walking on two legs, he
didn't look anything like the humans.

292
00:16:57,600 --> 00:17:00,880
And for some reason, his
nose was still blue as well.

293
00:17:01,080 --> 00:17:02,315
It looks like a yeti.

294
00:17:02,400 --> 00:17:03,857
It's dangerous, I'm sure.

295
00:17:03,940 --> 00:17:05,881
Get the children inside, quickly.

296
00:17:07,240 --> 00:17:09,197
A gun! Bring me a gun!

297
00:17:09,280 --> 00:17:10,280
Yeah, shoot him!

298
00:17:10,380 --> 00:17:13,360
Quick, before he runs
away! Get him! Shoot him!

299
00:17:14,340 --> 00:17:15,480
Yeah, I got him!

300
00:17:21,980 --> 00:17:23,460
Stay away from us, freak!

301
00:17:30,100 --> 00:17:31,920
He didn't know what was wrong.

302
00:17:32,100 --> 00:17:34,037
He couldn't understand
why they reacted to his

303
00:17:34,120 --> 00:17:37,900
appearance with so much fear
and anger stay away monster.

304
00:17:40,340 --> 00:17:42,597
He'd gone to the village
seeking friends but

305
00:17:42,680 --> 00:17:44,777
they called him a monster
and drove him away.

306
00:17:44,860 --> 00:17:47,297
He was no longer a reindeer but he wasn't

307
00:17:47,380 --> 00:17:49,909
a human either he was
something in between.

308
00:17:50,820 --> 00:17:55,761
And so he lived alone after that caught
between two worlds that wouldn't accept him.

309
00:17:56,400 --> 00:18:01,106
Now that you've heard his story do you
think you can heal the scar on his heart?

310
00:18:02,560 --> 00:18:05,217
Luffy, check out the door
at the front entrance.

311
00:18:05,300 --> 00:18:06,760
It's wide open. Huh?

312
00:18:10,720 --> 00:18:12,800
No wonder it's so cold in here.

313
00:18:13,420 --> 00:18:14,820
Anyway, let's close it.

314
00:18:15,000 --> 00:18:16,137
With it open like that,

315
00:18:16,220 --> 00:18:18,677
there's not much difference between
inside and outside the castle.

316
00:18:18,760 --> 00:18:19,590
Hey, stop it!

317
00:18:19,780 --> 00:18:20,917
Don't touch that door!

318
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:21,830
Get away!

319
00:18:23,820 --> 00:18:24,800
Never mind him.

320
00:18:24,920 --> 00:18:27,157
Let's close it, or we're
going to freeze to death.

321
00:18:27,240 --> 00:18:28,237
That's a good point.

322
00:18:28,320 --> 00:18:29,150
Stop!

323
00:18:29,233 --> 00:18:30,640
Did you guys hear what I said?

324
00:18:31,160 --> 00:18:32,040
Get back!

325
00:18:37,640 --> 00:18:39,200
What is with this guy?

326
00:18:39,440 --> 00:18:41,499
What the hell is he so angry about?

327
00:18:43,200 --> 00:18:45,140
Hey, come over here a second.

328
00:18:52,440 --> 00:18:53,400
Look up there.

329
00:19:02,340 --> 00:19:04,180
It's a bunch of baby snowbirds.

330
00:19:04,420 --> 00:19:06,773
See, if we closed the door, they'd fall.

331
00:19:06,940 --> 00:19:09,587
So that's the reason
they're leaving it open.

332
00:19:21,160 --> 00:19:22,120
It's freezing!

333
00:19:24,780 --> 00:19:26,660
Hold up a sec. Yeah?

334
00:19:27,800 --> 00:19:30,637
That weird reindeer guy,
wasn't he speaking earlier?

335
00:19:30,720 --> 00:19:34,544
Now that you mention it, I remember
him walking on two legs, too.

336
00:19:35,360 --> 00:19:36,600
He's a monster!

337
00:19:39,680 --> 00:19:41,560
Okay, let's get this straight.

338
00:19:41,840 --> 00:19:43,700
He walks upright and talks.

339
00:19:43,880 --> 00:19:44,880
But not human.

340
00:19:45,200 --> 00:19:46,720
Has fur. He's little.

341
00:19:46,920 --> 00:19:47,960
And becomes big.

342
00:19:48,720 --> 00:19:50,000
Clearly a monster!

343
00:20:04,940 --> 00:20:06,340
What a cool guy!

344
00:20:06,540 --> 00:20:09,940
I bet he's really interesting!
Hey, wait! I know!

345
00:20:10,240 --> 00:20:11,700
He should join us!
